          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "OUT",
          "page": "2/4, Microcontroller sheet"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "A status LED (D2) and series resistor (R3) are also on the HEATER net",
          "page": "Design specification, Heater path"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The indicator can show heater activation when the smart switch output is not actually delivering power, for example during a switch fault.",
      "confidence": 0.91
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The heater indicator is connected to the MCU control net rather than the smart switch output. It therefore reports the commanded state, not whether the heater output is active as specified."
}

